Where the skill's text names something the Windows build does otherwise, it says so: the default control socket path
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\ngterm\ngterm.sock` and how a socket path names the control pipe there (pass the path, never the
pipe), the config and state dirs (`%APPDATA%\ngterm`, `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ngterm`), the CLI on the user's PATH through the
installer or Install Command Line Tool…, and the overlay hide toggle's `ctrl+alt+shift+j` on Windows as on Linux.
`terminfo install` decompiles the compiled entry itself on every OS, since Windows has no `infocmp`
(`crates/ngterm-ctl/src/terminfo/source.rs`), so its text and its dump failure (`could not read <file>: <reason>`
where upstream's reads `infocmp exited N: <stderr>`) are this build's, and 128 plus the signal is a Unix exit.
